From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:33:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 301/310] Spatiand: what extensions keep in storage.sync, on
 every machine

Without Google's sync Chrome keeps an extension's storage.sync on the machine alone. It is now kept
in the shared folder as the Rust SpatiMesh kept it: profiles/<id>/extension-sync/<extension>/<key in
hex>.json, one file per key holding {"key", "value"}, so that two machines setting two keys while
apart both keep theirs. Every change to the area is told to SpatiMesh (StorageFrontend, a callback
of Spatiand's) and written there; every three seconds what another machine wrote is taken in,
through StorageFrontend, so that the extension's pages hear storage.onChanged. A key gone from the
folder that was in it was removed elsewhere; one set here before the folder had it goes into it.

Checked headless (2026-11-10) with an extension of a fixed key: storage.sync.set wrote both keys'
files; a key written into the folder, a value changed there and a file removed came back into the
extension's storage.sync within seconds, and its onChanged heard all three.
